{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>They shall be baked leavened.</b> Scripture commanded that they be leavened, because they are a thanksgiving offering to HaShem for that He has preserved for us the statutes of harvest, and the thanksgiving offering comes upon leavened bread. And perhaps the prohibition of leavened bread is because it alludes to the attribute of strict judgment, for it is called חָמֵץ just as wine that has soured is called חֹמֶץ יַיִן וְחֹמֶץ שֵׁכָר (Numbers 6:3), and the term is derived from the language of מְעַוֵּל וְחוֹמֵץ (Psalms 71:4), for their flavor is taken from them and they are not eaten. And likewise, כִּי יִתְחַמֵּץ לְבָבִי (Psalms 73:21) — he becomes angry and his reason is lost from him. And because the offerings are for a pleasing acceptance before the honored HaShem, they are not brought from things that possess the power to alter natures. And so they are not brought from things that are entirely sweet, such as honey, but only from things that are tempered, as they said concerning the creation of the world (Bereshit Rabbah 12:15): He partnered the attribute of mercy with the attribute of judgment and created it. Now on the festival of Shavuot, which is the day of the giving of the Torah, one fittingly brings the offering in the manner of a thanksgiving offering, for it is the day of Atzeret, and the enlightened will understand. And this is the secret of what our Rabbis said (Vayikra Rabbah 9:3): All offerings will cease, but the thanksgiving offering will never cease, etc. — for in it there is matzah and leavened bread, like the manner of the world to come."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The verse quoted as חֹמֶץ יַיִן וְחֹמֶץ שֵׁכָר appears in Numbers 6:3 as שֵׁכָר יֵין וְחֹמֶץ; Ramban inverts the order. The phrase מְעַוֵּל וְחוֹמֵץ in Psalms 71:4 is variously vocalized and parsed; translated here hyper-literally as Ramban reads it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:58:27.667389541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}